{title: In the Cross of Christ I Glory}
{artist: John Bowring / Ithamar Conkey}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: A}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 140}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The United Methodist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: The United Methodist Publishing House, 1989), # 295)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]In the cross of [E7]Christ I [A]glory,
[A]Tow[D]ering [A]o’er__[E]__ the [A]wrecks__[F#m]__ [B7]of [E]time;
[A]All the light of [E7]sacred [A]story
[A]Gathers round its head__[E7]__ sub[A]lime.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]When the woes of [E7]life o’er[A]take me—
[A]Hopes [D]de[A]ceive,__[E]__ and [A]fears__[F#m]__ [B7]ann[E]oy,
[A]Never shall the [E7]cross for[A]sake me,
[A]Lo! it glows with peace__[E7]__ and [A]joy.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]When the sun of [E7]bliss is [A]beaming
[A]Light [D]and [A]love__[E]__ up[A]on__[F#m]__ [B7]my [E]way,
[A]From the cross the [E7]radiance [A]streaming
[A]Adds more luster to__[E7]__ the [A]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[A]Bane and blessing, [E7]pain and [A]pleasure,
[A]By [D]the [A]cross__[E]__ are [A]sanc__[F#m]__[B7]ti[E]fied;
[A]Peace is there that [E7]knows no [A]measure,
[A]Joys that through all time__[E7]__ a[A]bide.
{end_of_verse}
